Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:21:37 -0400
Subject: feat: child tabs, and Arc's folders of folders come across whole

The owner's requests of the night of 2026-10-21, for 0.3.0 beta 2:

- Child tabs (docs/features/tabs.md R56-R59, settings T26; BACKLOG S-92):
  a link opened in a new tab (a middle click, Cmd-click, "Open link in new
  tab") or a page's own window.open becomes a child of the tab it came
  from (for window.open, the page that called it, not the tab on screen
  Chromium takes as the opener) and is drawn a level, 14 DIP, right of it in the sidebar, its pill
  and its contents both; a grandchild two levels. A row nests while every
  row between it and its parent descends from the parent, in the same
  folder or list; rows of another Space and rows in a collapsed folder take
  no part, and folders and children share one depth of 5. A new tab, a
  typed address, a bookmark, a duplicate and a drop are no one's child, and
  essentials and a Space's pins take none. Each parent gets a token and
  each child keeps its parent's, on the contents (carried through a jar
  change and a pin's reset) and in the session as per-tab extra data, so
  the tree survives a restart. A closed parent's children move up a level
  in its place. "Show tabs under the tab that opened them" in Settings >
  Stedding > Tabs, on by default, turns it off. Back closing a child at its
  first page is not built (R60).
- Import from Arc (import I3; BACKLOG S-48): an Arc list holding only lists
  was not made a folder, a folder needing tabs to be made around, so its
  folders came out a level up. It is now made around its first list's own
  tabs, that list's folder is made inside it, and the other lists follow.
  Found checking the owner's own import, which otherwise brought 8 of 8
  Spaces, 426 of 426 tabs and all 2,650 history rows.

Tests: TabParentsTest and TabParentsStripTest (the nesting rule, tokens,
restore, carry, a closed parent); ChildTabsTest (links, window.open, a new
tab, a duplicate, an essential, a background page's window, a closed
parent, a moved row, the setting, the session as a restart reads it); ArcSidebarImportWindowTest.
AFolderOfFoldersKeepsItsShape; SteddingPrefsTest for the new preference.

Why: the owner asked for child tabs, and the import check found the folders.
Removable when: never; the next re-cut gives child tabs a patch of its own
and folds the import fix into the importer's patch.
